  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe ₱5,000,000 standard deduction for estate tax is a tax-free threshold, not a deduction. It allows the estate to exclude this amount from the gross estate before calculating the estate tax due.\n\n### Interpretation\nThe ₱5,000,000 standard deduction serves as a threshold that reduces the taxable estate amount. It is not treated as a deduction in the traditional sense where expenses are subtracted from gross income; instead, it directly reduces the base on which the estate tax is calculated.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor estates valued at or below ₱5,000,000, this provision effectively means that no estate tax will be due, as the estate falls below the taxable threshold. For estates exceeding this amount, only the value above ₱5,000,000 will be subject to estate tax, simplifying the tax calculation for estates within this limit.",
